{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CevJDtHt4xsFUw9uPhztR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```\n<<PHASE:ANALYSIS>>\n```\n\n**Requirement, restated in one sentence:**\nAdd a `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` endpoint that transitions a CREATED shipment to CONFIRMED status (idempotent), rejects CANCELLED shipments with HTTP 409, and returns HTTP 404 for non-existent shipments.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n\n1. **Shipment model** — `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt:9-14` — data class with status field using ShipmentStatus enum (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n2. **ShipmentController** — `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt:20-56` — currently has create, getById, list endpoints; imports ResourceNotFoundException and ConflictException\n3. **InMemoryShipmentRepository** — `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentRepository.kt:10-27` — in-memory store with save(), findById(), existsById() methods\n4. **Exception handling** — `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiExceptions.kt:18-24` — ResourceNotFoundException (404) and ConflictException (409) are defined; `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:14-28` converts exceptions to ApiError envelope\n5. **ErrorCode enum** — `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt:31-37` — existing codes: ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED\n6. **Tests** — `sample-service/src/test/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — uses MockMvc to verify status codes and error codes in ApiError envelope\n\n**Conventions this repository already has:**\n\n- Controllers throw ApiExceptions (ResourceNotFoundException, ConflictException) which are caught by GlobalExceptionHandler\n- Error responses wrap error details in ApiError envelope with `code`, `message`, `fields`\n- Each domain scenario has its own ErrorCode (e.g., ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND)\n- POST endpoints return `ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CREATED).body(saved)` for success\n- Repository methods return nullable `Shipment?` and controller throws ResourceNotFoundException if null\n- Tests verify both happy path and error cases using MockMvc and jsonPath assertions\n\n**Affected files:**\n\n1. `ShipmentController.kt` — must add confirm endpoint that updates shipment status\n2. `ApiError.kt` — must add ErrorCode for state conflict (e.g., SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE) to distinguish this 409 from duplicates\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — must add tests for: confirm CREATED→CONFIRMED, confirm already CONFIRMED (idempotent), confirm CANCELLED (409), confirm missing (404)\n\n**Risks:**\n\n1. If I don't add a new ErrorCode, the 409 response will lack a machine-readable error code (violates the pattern where clients \"switch on a stable `code`\")\n2. Forgetting to persist the updated status to the repository\n3. Breaking idempotency if the code throws an error on repeated confirm of CONFIRMED shipment\n\n**Open questions:**\n\nWhich ErrorCode should be used for the 409 response when confirming a CANCELLED shipment? The ticket does not name one, but convention (ApiError.kt comment) suggests each scenario should have its own code. I will add `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` to the enum.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Add `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` to the ErrorCode enum to represent a 409 conflict when trying to confirm a shipment in a non-confirmable state (specifically CANCELLED).\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add a `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` method that:\n   - Retrieves the shipment by ID; if not found, throws ResourceNotFoundException with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throws ConflictException with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE\n   - If status is CREATED, updates it to CONFIRMED, persists via repository.save(), and returns it\n   - If status is already CONFIRMED, returns it unchanged (idempotent)\n   - Returns ResponseEntity.ok(shipment) for success (200, not 201)\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four test cases:\n   - `confirms a created shipment` — create S-1, confirm it, verify status changes to CONFIRMED\n   - `confirm already confirmed shipment succeeds` — create S-2, confirm twice, verify second call succeeds (200 OK) and shipment unchanged\n   - `rejects confirming a cancelled shipment` — write S-3 to repository with CANCELLED status directly, attempt confirm, verify 409 with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE code\n   - `rejects confirming missing shipment` — attempt confirm on non-existent S-99, verify 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n\n- **Adding no new ErrorCode** and reusing existing codes like VALIDATION_FAILED: Rejected because the ApiError.kt comment explicitly states \"add one deliberately\" for each scenario, and the existing pattern (ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS vs ORDER_NOT_FOUND) shows distinct codes per case. A 409 for state conflict is distinct from both 404 (missing) and 400 (invalid input).\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Write | Response | Mechanism |\n|------|------|-------|----------|-----------|\n| CREATED→CONFIRMED | repository.findById(id) | repository.save(copy with CONFIRMED) | 200 + Shipment | Success, return updated shipment |\n| Already CONFIRMED | repository.findById(id) | none | 200 + Shipment | Success, idempotent return |\n| CANCELLED | repository.findById(id) | none | 409 + ApiError(SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE) | ConflictException caught by GlobalExceptionHandler |\n| Missing | repository.findById(id) returns null | none | 404 + ApiError(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND) | ResourceNotFoundException caught by GlobalExceptionHandler |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n- **Test 1** (confirm CREATED): Verifies the happy path and state transition, checks status changes and response is 200\n- **Test 2** (confirm CONFIRMED idempotent): Verifies retry safety, checks second call succeeds and shipment state doesn't change\n- **Test 3** (confirm CANCELLED): Verifies state machine constraint, checks 409 status and error code (tests the new error code)\n- **Test 4** (confirm missing): Verifies standard 404 handling for non-existent resource\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes according to the design."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1383,"cache_read_input_tokens":16067,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1383},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d6cb5c94-0055-424d-9d31-0ec51c094c6d","uuid":"3350d8ad-442f-41f5-8f8f-eb5d654d9141","timestamp":"2026-09-10T19:18:49.293Z","request_id":"req_011CevJDseRcmcJj4FSnD931"}
